Files adapted from DataHub (each carries an attribution header):

- .claude/hooks/deny-git-no-verify.sh
    from .claude/hooks/deny-git-no-verify.sh (near-verbatim)
- .agent-skills/review/standards/python.md
    rule format ("if X, then flag it, with this title") from .cursor/BUGBOT.md;
    every rule is Trellis's own

The following patterns were re-implemented from scratch after reading DataHub; each module says so
in its docstring, and no code was copied:

- trellis_core.plugins        PluginRegistry and the metadata decorator
                              (datahub.ingestion.api.registry / .decorators)
- trellis_core.config         strict, secret-aware configuration base model
                              (datahub.configuration.common.ConfigModel)
- trellis_core.env_resolver   ${VAR} expansion in config files
                              (datahub.configuration.config_loader)
- trellis_core.report         bounded run reports and LossyList
                              (SourceReport, LossyList)
- trellis_core.instrumentation  ParamSpec + marker-attribute decorator
                              (telemetry.with_telemetry; the telemetry itself is not reproduced)
- trellis_events.pipeline.partition_executor  per-key ordered execution (PartitionExecutor)
- tests/integration           containers started and removed by the test session
                              (datahub.testing.docker_utils)
- .agent-skills/, .claude/    the agent-tooling layout: .agent-skills/<skill>/ with SKILL.md plus
                              standards/ templates/ scripts/ references/ and name/description
                              frontmatter, and a .claude/settings.json allowlist plus PreToolUse
                              hook (DataHub .agent-skills/, .claude/). The allowlist, the skills
                              and their contents are Trellis's own.

Any further file adapted from a third party keeps its own license and gets an attribution header
plus an entry in the list above.
